hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15631","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, meaning Ibn Umar, he said: Nafi informed me that he heard Abu Lubabah informing Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade killing snakes."
"15632","Affan narrated to us, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, he said: I heard Nafi saying: Ibn Umar used to order the killing of all snakes, leaving none of them, until Abu Lubabah al-Badri ibn Abd al-Mundhir narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade killing the snakes of houses."
"15633","Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr said: Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid al-Ansari, from Abi Lubabah al-Badri Ibn Abd al-Mundhir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The master of days is Friday, the greatest with Him, and the greatest with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, than the day of Fitr and the day of Adha, and in it are five characteristics: Allah created Adam in it, and Allah sent Adam down to earth in it, and in it Allah took Adam, and in it is an hour in which no servant asks anything except Allah, Blessed and Exalted, gives it to him, so long as he does not ask for unlawful, and in it the Hour will come. There is no angel near, nor heaven, nor earth, nor winds, nor mountains, nor sea, except they fear Friday."
